  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-02T17:29:04.912Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, VR users are able to change their keybinds, but Desktop users are not able to change their keybinds.\nFor example, if a player wants to change their gesture keys to a separate key, such as numpad, or unbind/rebind the safe mode because people may use it accidently, it would be a very useful tool.\nYou used to be able to change your keybinds on Desktop using the input menu from Unity, but this was removed, so now players are completely stuck with the default keybinds.\nI'm not sure why this feature was removed, because tons of other games, quite literally 90% of them, allow you to change your controls and keybinds. \nThis is really good feature for accessibility reasons as well, such as people who prefer to use arrow keys or IJKL instead of WASD.",
